A photograph can read the beacon

The matching runs on the boot thread again, and it takes a while: every
personality's start() may wait two seconds for a resource that is not
going to come.  The panel has to say whether that is movement or a stall,
and it could not: the number beside the heartbeat's letter changed every
time the shutter opened, so a photograph said nothing.

The letter keeps its beat.  The number beside it is written every
sixteenth time, and the beacon says how many rounds the matching has been
through, so a photograph says both whether it is alive and whether the
matching is moving.

